A query may start with FOR, UNWIND, LET, WITH, FILTER or RETURN. It then starts from one empty row (Gremlin's inject(0)): RETURN alone returns one row, FILTER keeps or drops it, FOR turns it into one row per item, and a later MATCH runs once for each row. g.gql("RETURN 1 + 2 AS three, upper('gql') AS up").to_list() // #{"three": 3, "up": "GQL"}
g.gql("RETURN count(*) AS c").to_list() // #{"c": 1}: the one empty row
g.gql("WITH 2 AS n RETURN n * n AS sq").to_list() // #{"sq": 4}
g.gql("FILTER $on RETURN 1 AS x", #{on: false}).to_list() // no row
g.gql("LET k = 30 MATCH (p:person) FILTER p.age > k RETURN p.name AS name ORDER BY name").to_list() // #{"name": "josh"}, #{"name": "peter"}

