CALL folder.name(args) is GQL's named procedure call: it runs the saved query name of the catalog folder folder (the segments before the name joined by /; one segment, CALL name(), calls a query of the root folder) for each incoming row , like a CALL { } body that imports nothing. Only saved queries written in GQL can be called. CALL f.name(a, b) YIELD x, y AS z [WHERE <condition>] -- inside a query: YIELD names the columns read after it
CALL f.name(a, b) -- inside a query, a VOID saved query (no RETURN): each row kept once
MATCH .. CALL f.name(a, b) -- a VOID call may end the query, like a write: zero rows
CALL f.name() YIELD n MATCH (n)-->(m) .. -- a yielded node (or edge) starts a later pattern
OPTIONAL CALL f.name(a) YIELD x -- keeps a row without results, with x NULL
CALL f.name(a, b) -- the whole query: every column of the saved query
CALL f.name(a, b) YIELD * -- the same
CALL f.name -- the whole query, arguments from the query's parameters by name The arguments are constants or $parameters (and lists, maps and arithmetic of them), positional in the order the saved query first reads its parameters; trailing ones left out take their defaults, and each is checked against the parameter's schema before the run. An argument that reads the row is not supported yet. YIELD names columns of the saved query's RETURN; each yielded name is a new variable (AS renames one, also swapping two names), and WHERE after the items filters the rows. Inside a query, a call of a saved query with columns needs YIELD; YIELD * and the form without parentheses are for a standalone call only. The saved query runs as a query of its own: it sees none of the caller's variables, and its variables none of the caller's. Its writes are part of the calling query's one unit. A call stands wherever a clause stands, also inside CALL { } bodies and UNION operands; inside EXISTS { }, COUNT { } and COLLECT { } it is not supported yet. The vendor namespaces db, dbms, apoc and gds are refused . g.define_query(#{ name: "older", folder: "people", language: "gql", params: #{min: #{schema: #{type: "integer"}, default: 30}}, body: "MATCH (p:person) WHERE p.age > $min RETURN p.name AS name, p.age AS age"
});
g.gql("MATCH (s:software) CALL people.older(33) YIELD name RETURN s.name AS sw, name ORDER BY sw").to_list();
// [#{"name": "peter", "sw": "lop"}, #{"name": "peter", "sw": "ripple"}]
g.gql("MATCH (s:software) OPTIONAL CALL people.older(40) YIELD name RETURN s.name AS sw, name ORDER BY sw").to_list();
// [#{"name": (), "sw": "lop"}, #{"name": (), "sw": "ripple"}]
g.gql("CALL people.older(26) YIELD name RETURN name UNION CALL people.older(33) YIELD name RETURN name").to_list();
// marko, vadas, josh, peter
g.gql("CALL people.older").to_list(); // [#{"age": 32, "name": "josh"}, #{"age": 35, "name": "peter"}]: min takes its default 30 .profile() shows a call as gql:call_query("people/older", ..) with the saved query's plan as its child. Saved Queries has the parameters, VOID queries, effects and permissions; Errors every error of a call.

