Kind Forms literals integers (42, 1_000, 0x1F, 0o17, 0b101), floats (1.5, .5, 1.5e3), strings ('...' or "..."), TRUE, FALSE, NULL, lists [1, 2], maps (records) {k: v}, also written RECORD {k: v} parameters $name ( Parameters ) property access n.name, m.key on a map indexing and slicing x[0], x[-1], x[1..3], x[..2], x[1..], m['key'], n[k] (Cypher, below ) comparison =, <> (Cypher !=), <, <=, >, >=; a chain a < b <= c is the Cypher compatibility form of a < b AND b <= c ( alias ) logic AND, OR, XOR, NOT predicates IS [NOT] NULL, IN [list], STARTS WITH, ENDS WITH, CONTAINS, IS [NOT] LABELED, IS [NOT] SOURCE OF e, IS [NOT] DESTINATION OF e arithmetic +, -, *, /, %, ^ (Cypher power, always a float: 2 ^ 10 is 1024.0), unary - and + concatenation || on two strings or two lists (Cypher +); Cypher + of a list and one other value appends or prepends it ([1] + 2 is [1, 2], 0 + [1] is [0, 1]) conditional simple CASE x WHEN v THEN r ... ELSE d END and searched CASE WHEN cond THEN r ... END conversion CAST(x AS INTEGER | FLOAT | STRING | BOOLEAN) ( Conversions ) function calls name(args) ( Functions ) map projection p {.name, .*, f, key: expr} (Cypher, below ) list comprehension [x IN list WHERE cond | expr], either part optional (Cypher) pattern comprehension [(p)-[:knows]->(f) WHERE cond | expr] (Cypher) Precedence, loosest first: OR, XOR, AND, NOT, comparison, the predicates (IS NULL, IN, STARTS WITH, ...), + - ||, * / %, ^ (left to right: 2 ^ 3 ^ 2 is 64.0), unary minus (-3 ^ 2 is 9.0), property access and subscripts (x[i], x[a..b], left to right: [1, 2][0] + 1 is 2). x ^ y follows the rules of power(x, y): 0 ^ -1 and (-8) ^ 0.5 are errors (2201F), an overflow is error 22003. g.gql("MATCH (n:person) WHERE n.age IN [27, 35] RETURN n.name AS name ORDER BY name").to_list() // #{"name": "peter"}, #{"name": "vadas"}
g.gql("MATCH (n:person) WHERE n.name STARTS WITH 'm' OR n.name ENDS WITH 's' OR n.name CONTAINS 'et' RETURN n.name AS name ORDER BY name").to_list() // marko, peter, vadas
g.gql("MATCH (n:person) WHERE n.age > 30 XOR n.name = 'josh' RETURN n.name AS name ORDER BY name").to_list() // #{"name": "peter"}
g.gql("MATCH (n:person) RETURN n.name || '!' AS a, n.age * 2 + 1 AS b, n.age / 10 AS c, n.age % 10 AS d, n.age / 10.0 AS e ORDER BY a LIMIT 1").to_list()
// #{"a": "josh!", "b": 65, "c": 3, "d": 2, "e": 3.2}
g.gql("MATCH (n:person) RETURN n.name AS name, CASE WHEN n.age < 30 THEN 'young' WHEN n.age < 34 THEN 'middle' ELSE 'senior' END AS band ORDER BY name").to_list()
// josh middle, marko young, peter senior, vadas young
g.gql("MATCH (n) RETURN n.name AS name, CASE n.lang WHEN 'java' THEN 'jvm' ELSE 'other' END AS k ORDER BY name LIMIT 2").to_list()
// #{"k": "other", "name": "josh"}, #{"k": "jvm", "name": "lop"}
g.gql("MATCH (n:person) RETURN {name: n.name, tags: [n.age, NULL, true]} AS m ORDER BY n.name LIMIT 1").to_list()
// #{"m": #{"name": "josh", "tags": [32, (), true]}}
g.gql("MATCH (n:person) RETURN RECORD {name: n.name, age: n.age} AS m ORDER BY n.name LIMIT 1").to_list()
// #{"m": #{"age": 32, "name": "josh"}} RECORD {k: v} is the ISO record constructor with its keyword written out; it builds the same map as {k: v}. The word is contextual, not reserved: RECORD (any case) followed by { and then } or name: is the constructor; anywhere else record is an ordinary variable, also before a map projection such as record {.name}. A variable named record whose projection is empty or starts with a key: expr item is back-quoted: `record` {k: 1}. Integer arithmetic stays integer (/ truncates toward zero, % takes the sign of the dividend); a float operand makes the result a float. An overflow or an integer division by zero is an error, never a wrapped value ( Errors ); a float divided by zero follows IEEE 754 (1.0 / 0.0 is Infinity, 0.0 / 0.0 is NaN; Semantics ). g.gql("RETURN [1, 2] + 3 AS a, 0 + [1] AS b, [1] + [2] AS c").to_list() // #{"a": [1, 2, 3], "b": [0, 1], "c": [1, 2]}

