Function names are case-insensitive (toInteger, TOINTEGER). Every function returns NULL for a NULL argument (except coalesce, nullif and the ...OrNull conversions, by their definition) and fails for an argument of the wrong kind (22G03), never with a silent NULL. A position or a length counts characters (Unicode scalar values), never bytes. The aggregates are listed under Aggregation ; Semantics has the exact rules and where they differ from Neo4j and from the Gremlin steps of the same name. The functions come from two sources: the GQL functions (with their Cypher spellings as aliases ), and a fixed list of openCypher compatibility functions that GQL has no counterpart for (toInteger, substring, split, round, keys, nodes, ...): they keep their Neo4j meaning ( Cypher Aliases ). Function Returns Cypher alias element_id(x) the id of a vertex or edge, a string elementId(x) labels(x) a vertex's labels in stored order (primary first); an edge's label as a one-item list type(e) an edge's label; a vertex is an error (use labels(v)) coalesce(a, b, ...) the first argument that is not NULL nullif(a, b) NULL when a = b is TRUE, else a same (nullIf) path_length(p) the number of edges of a path length(p) g.gql("MATCH (n) RETURN element_id(n) AS id, labels(n) AS labels ORDER BY id LIMIT 3").to_list()
// #{"id": "1", "labels": ["person"]}, #{"id": "2", "labels": ["person"]}, #{"id": "3", "labels": ["software"]}
g.gql("MATCH ()-[e]->() RETURN element_id(e) AS id, type(e) AS type, e.weight AS w ORDER BY id LIMIT 2").to_list()
// #{"id": "0", "type": "knows", "w": 0.5}, #{"id": "1", "type": "created", "w": 0.4}
g.gql("MATCH (n) RETURN n.name AS name, coalesce(n.age, n.lang) AS info ORDER BY name LIMIT 2").to_list()
// #{"info": 32, "name": "josh"}, #{"info": "java", "name": "lop"}
g.gql("MATCH (n:person) RETURN n.name AS name, nullif(n.age, 29) AS age ORDER BY name").to_list()
// #{"age": 32, "name": "josh"}, #{"age": (), "name": "marko"}, #{"age": 35, "name": "peter"}, #{"age": 27, "name": "vadas"}

