GQL's CAST is strict : text that is not a value of the target type is an error (22018). The Cypher conversions are lenient : toInteger, toFloat, toBoolean give NULL for such text, and their ...OrNull forms give NULL for a value of any unsupported kind too ( Semantics ). Function Converts Unconvertible text Wrong kind CAST(x AS INTEGER) (INT, INT64, BIGINT, SIGNED INTEGER) integer; float truncated toward zero; a decimal text ('42', ' 1.9 ', '1e3') error 22018 error 22G03 (a boolean too) CAST(x AS FLOAT) (FLOAT64, DOUBLE, DOUBLE PRECISION, REAL) number; a decimal text, 'NaN', 'Infinity', '-Infinity' error 22018 error 22G03 CAST(x AS STRING) (VARCHAR, CHAR VARYING) any value except a vertex, edge or path - error 22G03 CAST(x AS BOOLEAN) (BOOL) boolean; 'true' / 'false' in any case, 'unknown' is NULL error 22018 error 22G03 (numbers too) toInteger(x) as CAST, also true / false (1 / 0) and Cypher literals ('0x1F', '0o17', '1_000') NULL error 22G03 toFloat(x) as CAST, also Cypher literals NULL error 22G03 toBoolean(x) as CAST, also integers (0 is FALSE, any other TRUE) NULL error 22G03 toString(x) as CAST(x AS STRING), scalars only; a temporal value in Neo4j's text ( Dates and times ) - error 22G03 (a list or a map too) toIntegerOrNull(x), toFloatOrNull(x), toBooleanOrNull(x), toStringOrNull(x) as their toX NULL NULL (for toStringOrNull a list, map, vertex, edge or path too) A float's text always shows that it is a float (toString(1.0) is '1.0', Neo4j's form), while Gremlin's as_string() gives "1"; integers and booleans give the same text as as_string(). A list or a map converts to Neo4j's text form ('[29, marko, 1.0, null]', '{a: 1, b: marko}'). g.gql("MATCH (n:person) RETURN n.name AS name, toString(n.age) AS a, toString(n.age / 10.0) AS b ORDER BY name").to_list()
// #{"a": "32", "b": "3.2", "name": "josh"}, #{"a": "29", "b": "2.9", "name": "marko"}, #{"a": "35", "b": "3.5", "name": "peter"}, #{"a": "27", "b": "2.7", "name": "vadas"}
g.v().has_label("person").values("age").as_string().order().to_list() // "27", "29", "32", "35"
g.gql("MATCH (n:person) RETURN toFloat(n.age) AS f ORDER BY f").to_list() // #{"f": 27.0}, #{"f": 29.0}, #{"f": 32.0}, #{"f": 35.0}
g.v().has_label("person").values("age").as_number(GType.DOUBLE).order().to_list() // 27.0, 29.0, 32.0, 35.0
g.gql("MATCH (n:person {name: 'marko'}) RETURN CAST('42' AS INTEGER) AS i, CAST(' 1.5 ' AS FLOAT) AS f, CAST('TRUE' AS BOOLEAN) AS b, CAST(1.0 AS STRING) AS s").to_list()
// #{"b": true, "f": 1.5, "i": 42, "s": "1.0"}
g.gql("MATCH (n:person {name: 'marko'}) RETURN toInteger(' 42 ') AS a, toInteger('1.9') AS b, toInteger('0x1F') AS c, toInteger('abc') AS d, toIntegerOrNull(true) AS e").to_list()
