CALL folder.name(args) [YIELD ..] ( Calling saved queries ) runs a saved GQL query as a query of its own for each incoming row, like a CALL { } body that imports nothing; Neo4j's procedures are its model, with these differences, each a deliberate decision: Constant arguments. An argument is a constant or a $parameter (lists, maps and arithmetic of them included), evaluated once when the query is compiled; Neo4j also takes expressions over the row. So arity, types and missing parameters are errors before the run, and the called query is planned once with its argument values. An argument that reads the row is 0A000 (not yet). Saved GQL queries only. A procedure is a saved query of the graph's catalog written in GQL; one written in Rhai is 0A000 (call it with g.query(..) from the DSL), and the vendor namespaces db, dbms, apoc and gds are refused (CALL db.labels()). Names are unique across folders. The folder of CALL a.b.name() must be a/b exactly (CALL name() is the root folder); since a saved query's name is unique in the whole catalog, a name found in another folder is an error with a "did you mean", never a second procedure. Positional order. The arguments bind the parameters in the order the saved query first reads them (g.get_query(name)["params"]), not in a declared signature order. Schema coercion. An argument is checked and coerced by its parameter's schema, as a write is: an integer passed for a number parameter arrives as a float (42 becomes 42.0), where Neo4j's NUMBER keeps the integer. No commit attribute. The called query's writes are part of the calling query's one unit; unlike g.query(..) of a query that writes, the commit carries no attribute naming the saved query and its arguments. Not inside EXISTS, COUNT or COLLECT yet. A call stands wherever a clause stands, also in CALL { } bodies and UNION operands, but not yet in those subquery bodies (0A000). g.define_query(#{name: "sw", language: "gql", body: "MATCH (s:software) RETURN s"});
g.define_query(#{name: "half", language: "gql", params: #{x: "number"}, body: "RETURN $x AS x, $x / 2 AS h"});
g.gql("CALL sw() YIELD s RETURN s.name AS n, labels(s) AS l ORDER BY n").to_list();
// [#{"l": ["software"], "n": "lop"}, #{"l": ["software"], "n": "ripple"}]
g.gql("CALL sw() YIELD s MATCH (s)<-[:created]-(p) RETURN s.name AS s, count(p) AS n ORDER BY s").to_list();
// [#{"n": 3, "s": "lop"}, #{"n": 1, "s": "ripple"}]: a yielded node starts a later pattern
g.gql("CALL half(5)").to_list(); // [#{"h": 2.5, "x": 5.0}]: the integer 5 arrives as 5.0

