GQL's CAST and Cypher's toInteger / toFloat / toBoolean / toString share one set of conversion rules and differ in what an unconvertible value gives: Case CAST(x AS T) toX(x) toXOrNull(x) a text that is no value of the type ('abc' to INTEGER) error 22018 NULL NULL a value of a kind the type does not take (true to FLOAT) error 22G03 error 22G03 NULL a number out of range (1.0e19 to INTEGER) error 22003 error 22003 NULL a list or a map to STRING its text error 22G03 NULL a vertex, edge or path to STRING error 22G03 error 22G03 NULL To INTEGER: a float is truncated toward zero (1.9 is 1, -1.9 is -1); a text is a decimal number, also with a fraction or an exponent, truncated the same way ('1.9' is 1, '1e3' is 1000, computed exactly, without a float in between). toInteger also reads Cypher integer literals ('0x1F' is 31, '0o11' is 9, '1_000' is 1000) and true / false as 1 / 0; CAST reads decimal text only, and a boolean is 22G03. To FLOAT: a decimal number, 'NaN', 'Infinity', '-Infinity'; toFloat also reads Cypher literals. Java-only forms ('1.5f', '1d', hexadecimal floats) are not numbers. To BOOLEAN: 'true' and 'false' in any letter case; CAST reads 'unknown' as NULL; toBoolean takes an integer too (0 is FALSE, every other integer TRUE), CAST does not. To STRING: an integer, UUID or date gives the same text as Gremlin's as_string(); a float always shows a decimal point or an exponent, in Neo4j's (Java's) form: '1.0', '3.2', '1.0E7', '1.0E-4', '1.5E20' (plain decimal from 0.001 up to 10 000 000); booleans give 'true' / 'false'; CAST of a list or map gives Neo4j's text ('[1, a, true, null]', '{a: 1, b: hi}', strings unquoted), while toString takes scalars only, as in Neo4j (a list or map is 22G03, toStringOrNull gives NULL; stage 3f, the openCypher TCK TypeConversion4). Surrounding blanks: CAST skips spaces around the text; the Cypher forms skip every character up to U+0020 (spaces, tabs, line breaks), as Java's String.trim() does, and toBoolean any Java whitespace. g.gql("MATCH (n:person {name: 'marko'}) RETURN toString(1.0) AS a, toString(1.5e20) AS b, toString(0.0001) AS c, toString(10000000.0) AS d").to_list()
// #{"a": "1.0", "b": "1.5E20", "c": "1.0E-4", "d": "1.0E7"}
g.inject(1.0).as_string().to_list() // "1": Gremlin's text of a float
g.gql("MATCH (n:person {name: 'marko'}) RETURN toInteger('1.9') AS a, toInteger('0x1F') AS b, toIntegerOrNull('0x1F') AS c").to_list() // #{"a": 1, "b": 31, "c": 31}
g.inject("1.9").as_number(GType.LONG).to_list() // error: Gremlin's as_number(GType.LONG) does not read a fraction in text
g.gql("MATCH (n:person {name: 'marko'}) RETURN CAST('0x1F' AS INTEGER) AS x") // error: invalid character value for cast (22018)
