Item Column name expr AS name name n.name without AS the expression text as written: n.name count(*) without AS the same rule: count(*) RETURN * every named variable, in name order (code point order, as Neo4j: a, b, p; WITH * too) RETURN *, expr AS x the variables first, then x A name used twice is an error. Give every computed column an AS name: it is easier to read and to reach from Gremlin (select("name")), and the text form of an unaliased column follows Neo4j's rule today (the expression as written), which may still be aligned with the ISO naming rule. g.gql("MATCH (p:person) RETURN p.name ORDER BY p.name LIMIT 2").to_list() // #{"p.name": "josh"}, #{"p.name": "marko"}
g.gql("MATCH (s:software) RETURN s.name AS `the name` ORDER BY `the name`").to_list() // #{"the name": "lop"}, #{"the name": "ripple"}
g.gql("MATCH (n:person) RETURN n.age AS a, n.name AS a") // error: the column name `a` is used twice in RETURN A keyword (by, order, match, ...) is fine as a label, a property key or an AS name, but where it is read back as a variable (in ORDER BY, or as a pattern variable) it must be back-quoted: RETURN p.name AS by ORDER BY `by` .

