A path variable (RETURN p) and a group variable (the variable of a quantified edge, or a variable inside a quantified path pattern) hold elements, so Gremlin can continue from them too: Column Value JSON a path variable p a path: vertex, edge, vertex, ..., in the written order (Gremlin's path() value) a list of the element objects a group variable e of -[e]->{1,3} a list of the edges, in the written order; [] for a zero-length match a list of edge objects a group variable x or e of ((x)-[e]->(y)){1,3} a list of the nodes or edges, one per iteration in the written order; [] for zero iterations (with ?: the single element, or NULL) a list of element objects either, from an OPTIONAL MATCH that did not match NULL null g.gql("MATCH p = (a {name: 'marko'})-[:knows]->(b {name: 'vadas'}) RETURN p").to_list() // #{"p": [v[1], e[0][1-knows->2], v[2]]}
g.gql("MATCH p = (a {name: 'marko'})-[:knows]->(b {name: 'vadas'}) RETURN p").to_json()
// [{"p": [{"id": "1", "label": "person", ...}, {"id": "0", "label": "knows", "inV": "2", "outV": "1", ...}, {"id": "2", ...}]}]
g.gql("MATCH p = (a {name: 'marko'})-[:knows]->(b {name: 'vadas'}) RETURN p").select("p").unfold().to_list() // v[1], e[0][1-knows->2], v[2]
g.v().has("name", "marko").out_e("knows").in_v().has("name", "vadas").path().to_list() // [v[1], e[0][1-knows->2], v[2]]

