REMOVE takes comma-separated items like SET: REMOVE n.k removes a property of a node or an edge, REMOVE n:A (also REMOVE n IS A, REMOVE n:A:B) removes labels from a node, and the last label may go too. Removing what is not there changes nothing, and a NULL target is skipped. g.gql("MATCH (p:person {name: 'marko'}) REMOVE p.age RETURN keys(p) AS keys").to_list() // #{"keys": ["name"]}
