g.gql("MATCH (p:person {name: 'marko'}) REMOVE p.nothing, p:nothing RETURN labels(p) AS labels, keys(p) AS keys").to_list() // #{"keys": ["name", "age"], "labels": ["person"]} The same in Gremlin: g.v().has("name", "marko").property("age", 30).add_label("admin").values("age").next() // 30
g.v().has("name", "marko").remove_property("age").properties().key().to_list() // "name"
g.v().has("name", "ripple").add_label("product").drop_label("software").label().next() // "product"

